{
  "comment": "MOCK DATA, not wired into the site. How long each skill was used, in years, at each job. No self-ratings. Three ways to state a use, most precise first: (1) 'from'/'to' actual years; (2) 'years' plus 'when' (start, middle, end) for where it sat in the job; (3) 'years' alone, assumed to overlap the job's other skills, so a category takes the longest rather than the sum. Categories are flat and a skill can belong to several ('scss' is both Styling and Frontend). A skill may have a 'parent' when it is part of another ('C# Web API' inside 'C#'): categories count parents, children add detail. Caps: a skill can't outlast its job, and a total can't outlast the real calendar span of the jobs it came from. Own-studio work (including this site) sits under StormScape. Run: npm run skills:report",
